{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QJucysMurphyEigen","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SytContentTuple"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.heckeWedderburn_symm_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.heckeWedderburn_symm_single","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L436-L444","doc":"**The inverse Wedderburn map on a matrix unit is an explicit polynomial in the `σ_i`.**\n`(heckeWedderburn q)⁻¹ (E^λ_{TT}) = jmProjIn q σ (contentVec T)`, whose coefficients are rational\nfunctions of `q` with denominators the differences `[c]_{q²} − [d]_{q²}`, `|c|, |d| ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.heckeProduct_jmProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.heckeProduct_jmProj","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L388-L434","doc":"**The seminormal product sends the JM projector of `T` to the matrix unit `E^λ_{TT}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.eq_of_contentVec_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.eq_of_contentVec_eq","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L374-L379","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.shape_eq_of_contentVec_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.shape_eq_of_contentVec_eq","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L355-L372","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projVal_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projVal_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L341-L349","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projVal_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projVal_self","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L325-L338","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.seminormalRep_jmProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.seminormalRep_jmProj","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L300-L322","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.projVal","kind":"def","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L294-L298","doc":"The scalar the projector takes on the seminormal vector `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.seminormalRep_jmAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.seminormalRep_jmAdd","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L279-L292","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.contentVec_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.contentVec_mem","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L265-L270","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.contentVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.contentVec","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L261-L263","doc":"The content vector `k ↦ c(T(k+1))` of a standard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.cellContent_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.cellContent_bound","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L233-L259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.list_prod_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.list_prod_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L220-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.map_jmProjIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.map_jmProjIn","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L202-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmProjIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmProjIn","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L198-L200","doc":"The **JM projector** attached to a content vector `c`: `∏_{k ≤ n} jmFactorIn k (c k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmFactorIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmFactorIn","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L193-L196","doc":"The `k`-th Lagrange factor `∏_{d ≠ c, |d| ≤ n} (Y_k − [d])/([c] − [d])`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.mem_contentRange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.mem_contentRange","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L187-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.contentRange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.contentRange","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L184-L185","doc":"The integers `−n, …, n`, as a list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.sq_sub_one_smul_jmAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.sq_sub_one_smul_jmAdd","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L155-L174","doc":"**`(q² − 1)·Y_k = L_k − 1`** in `H_{n+1}(q)`, for every `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAdd","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L151-L153","doc":"The additive JM elements of the Hecke algebra itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.map_jmAddIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.map_jmAddIn","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L140-L149","doc":"Algebra maps commute with the recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAddIn_succ_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAddIn_succ_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L136-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAddIn_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAddIn_succ","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L132-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAddIn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.jmAddIn","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L122-L130","doc":"The **additive Jucys–Murphy elements** in any `K`-algebra `A` carrying `n` \"generators\" `g`:\n`Y_0 = 0`, `Y_{k+1} = g_k Y_k g_k + q⁻¹ g_k`. With `g = σ` in `H_{n+1}(q)` this is\n`(L_k − 1)/(q² − 1)` (`sq_sub_one_smul_jmAdd`), but the recursion itself has no denominator\n`q² − 1`, so it is defined — and polynomial in the `g_i` with coefficients in `ℤ[q⁻¹]` — at every\n`q ≠ 0`, including `q = 1`, where it is the classical `Y_{k+1} = s_k Y_k s_k + s_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_one_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_one_injective","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L109-L112","doc":"At `q = 1` the `q²`-integers are the integers, so again injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_injective","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L97-L107","doc":"At a parameter that is not a root of unity, `c ↦ [c]_{q²}` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2_one","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L89-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.sq_sub_one_mul_qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.sq_sub_one_mul_qInt2","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L65-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.JMProjector.qInt2","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/JMProjector.lean#L58-L63","doc":"The signed `q²`-integer `[c]_{q²}`: `1 + q² + ⋯ + q^{2(c−1)}` for `c ≥ 0`, and\n`−(q^{−2} + ⋯ + q^{2c})` for `c < 0`. It is the unique Laurent polynomial with\n`(q² − 1)·[c]_{q²} = q^{2c} − 1`, and `[c]_1 = c`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}